[Music]  hi guys it's quinn here if you enjoy my  videos consider hitting the like button  it's the only way the youtube algorithm  really notices me  today we will be discussing the blind  site by peter watts  now we as humans tend to view  evolution in a very  self-centralizing way we tend to imagine  that the most intelligent species will  be the most dominant species  we tend to imagine that a species  evolving equals a species becoming  smarter  but scientifically that's obviously not  the case the most successful species on  this planet are not intelligent in the  slightest we are so used to seeing  depictions of alien civilizations that  are different from us but still in some  way fundamentally like us  operating based on at least some form of  reason operating based on some form of  comprehension we assume that in order  for a species to travel the stars  intelligence is necessary so therefore  we assume that most if not all  space-faring civilizations  would be  to some degree  intelligent but if we truly think about  this reasonably  wouldn't exactly the opposite be true  the human brain is a tremendous resource  cost for our body other animals don't  have to worry about growing a huge brain  so they can put resources in other  places like reproduction which is  technically the goal of life when we  talk about what makes a species  successful the answer is not  intelligence plenty of intelligent  animals have gone extinct a good  measurement of the success of a species  is the population and the quality of  life and we all know that humanity has a  unique propensity for suffering that is  thanks to intelligence  so the blind site spoilers ahead by the  way  provides an interesting and rather  devastating idea  what if humanity  is just a fluke  now i should say that intelligence is  not precisely  the issue here the issue is self  awareness specifically  a creature could potentially be highly  intelligent while completely and utterly  lacking consciousness  completely and utterly lacking  self-awareness  so in essence  a step is cut out consciousness  gets in the way consciousness slows the  process  i waste energy and processing power  self obsesses to the point of psychosis  scramblers have no need of it  scramblers are more parsimonious  with simpler biochemistries  with smaller brains deprived of tools of  their ship even parts of their own  metabolism they think rings around you  they hide their language in plain sight  even when you know what they're saying  they turn your own cognition against  itself they travel between the stars  this is what intelligence can do on  hampered by self-awareness  so the scramblers who we encounter in  the blind site are the first  extraterrestrials that humankind has  ever come into contact with and they're  not conscious at all  but they have  several orders of magnitude more brain  power than human beings  but they use that brain power to operate  their exceptionally complex sensory  organs and musculature system  they're extremely fast extremely  reactive and formidable so  an interesting concept that this book  introduced me to is the concept of the  chinese room  now this book itself recognizes that the  actual idea of a chinese room is  actually a fallacy but for the purposes  of understanding this section of the  story the concept is adequate  imagine a man in a room and through a  hole in a wall he is being given pieces  of paper with symbols on them and he  also has access to a database of symbols  just like the ones that come through the  wall and rules that tell him how to put  those symbols together but the point is  he still doesn't have any idea what all  these symbols are or what information  they contain he only knows that when he  encounters a certain symbol he is to  respond with this set of rules involving  this set of symbols  now if you've ever heard of the turing  test this idea was originally thought to  be  the counter to the turing test now this  story brings up this idea in an  extremely creepy context for a while the  crew of the spaceship theses are  attempting to communicate with the alien  vessel they refer to it as rorschach and  the alien vessel is responding to them  in a human voice  so eventually they realize that the  voice that they're talking to  actually is a chinese room but what's  really creepy about it is how closely  this chinese room  resembles  actual comprehension  actual understanding  oh right rorschach said suddenly  we get it now  you don't think there's anyone here do  you  you've got some high-priced consultant  telling you there's nothing to worry  about jack was deep in the forest we'd  lost most of the tactical overlays to  reduce to bod in the dim visible light  rorschach's crate rigid spines each the  size of a skyscraper hashed a nightmare  view on all sides the feed stuttered as  baits struggled to keep the beam aligned  consensus painted walls and airspace  with arcane telemetry i had no idea what  any of it meant  you think we're nothing but a chinese  room rorschach sneered jack stumbled  towards collision grasping for something  to hang on to  your mistake theseus  the ship rorschach itself is also  terrifying it's described as like a  giant crown of thorns twisted and dark  and unreflective and just like way too  tangled to ever actually go on  somebody's head and also absolutely  giant with spikes the size of  skyscrapers so the combination of the  image of that vessel and the creepy  unnerving voice that's being transmitted  from it makes for really great horror in  my opinion  and this book has other really awesome  elements of horror for instance in this  book vampires actually existed at some  point during human history they were an  offshoot of humans that became predatory  towards other humans but they also had  this ability to go into hibernation for  long periods of time so actually in this  series they're able to through  biological engineering bring back  vampires and actually create hybrid  humans that actually have some of the  hibernation abilities of those vampires  one of the crew members of the ship  theseus saresti is actually a vampire  and he makes the other crew members very  nervous because at any time he could  revert back to his primal instincts and  decide to prey upon them so not only is  there this ominous extraterrestrial  threat from the outside there's also a  potential threat on the inside this book  also goes into other concepts like  self-hood and the idea of consciousness  being uploaded into a cloud it has many  of the great elements that i really just  love in science fiction so i definitely  would recommend this book to you guys if  you enjoy these elements and stories as  well there's also the sequel echopraxia  which i plan on covering at some point  in the future as well thank you guys so  much for watching make sure you like and  subscribe for more quinn's ideas  just a heads up for those of you that  may be interested my next graphic novel  the lie behind the star is launching  february 2023 you can sign up now to get  on the email mailing list to get  notified as soon as it launches more  information on my website link in the  description thank you guys so much  [Music]  you

